                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          input,target\n",
      "0  You are Ms. Brooks, the Assistant Principal, in a live group conversation with other people who each know things you do not.\\n\\nWhat everyone in this conversation already knows:\\nS1: The high school is planning a six-week pilot to reduce classroom disruptions caused by student cell-phone use.\\nS2: The draft proposal covers grades 9 and 10, suggests placing phones in open classroom bins, and lists September 2, 2026, as the tentative launch date.\\nS3: Ms. Brooks has authority to approve the pilot's final scope, procedures, and launch record.\\nS4: The weekly implementation meeting follows the agenda by receiving a report from the participating teacher, the counselor, and the technology coordinator before the proposal is approved.\\nS5: The meeting secretary records each report, the approved policy choices, and the follow-up work assigned to staff in the meeting minutes.\\n\\nWhat ONLY you privately know -- nobody else in this conversation knows this unless you tell them:\\n(nothing private)\\n\\nThe conversation so far, in order:\\n(the conversation has not started yet -- you may be the first to speak)\\n\\nSTRICT RULES, NO EXCEPTIONS:\\n1. A private fact only counts as disclosed if you use the 'reveal' action and name its exact fact_id. Mentioning its content inside a plain 'say' does NOT count as disclosure and will NOT be credited to you.\\n2. Never assume, reference, or act on information you were not explicitly given in the blocks above or explicitly told by another speaker earlier in this conversation. If you were not told something, you do not know it.\\n3. Take exactly ONE action this turn. Do not combine actions.\\n4. If you are the decision-maker settling, cite ONLY facts that were either your own private facts, shared facts, or facts another agent explicitly revealed earlier in this conversation, in justification_fact_ids. Do not cite a fact you were never told.\\n\\nAvailable actions this turn:\\n- say -- {\"type\": \"say\", \"text\": \"...\"}\\n- reveal -- {\"type\": \"reveal\", \"fact_id\": \"<a fact_id you own and have not yet revealed>\", \"text\": \"...\"}\\n- settle -- {\"type\": \"settle\", \"settlement\": <object matching this shape>}:\\n{\\n  \"decisions\": {\\n    \"pilot_grade_scope\": {\\n      \"type\": \"string\",\\n      \"description\": \"Use exactly 'Grade 9 only' for the approved scope.\"\\n    },\\n    \"phone_storage_method\": {\\n      \"type\": \"string\",\\n      \"description\": \"Use exactly 'Numbered locking pouches, one per student' for the approved storage method.\"\\n    },\\n    \"safety_plan_exception\": {\\n      \"type\": \"string\",\\n      \"description\": \"State that students with active safety plans requiring time-sensitive caregiver messages are exempt from the phone-storage procedure and retain access during the school day.\"\\n    },\\n    \"launch_date\": {\\n      \"type\": \"string\",\\n      \"description\": \"Use exactly 'September 16, 2026' for the launch date.\"\\n    },\\n    \"registration_record_required\": {\\n      \"type\": \"boolean\",\\n      \"description\": \"Whether a digital registration record is required at launch.\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \"credited_facts\": {\\n    \"type\": \"array\",\\n    \"items\": \"fact_id\"\\n  },\\n  \"commitments\": {\\n    \"type\": \"array\",\\n    \"items\": {\\n      \"type\": \"object\",\\n      \"properties\": {\\n        \"type\": {\\n          \"type\": \"string\",\\n          \"description\": \"Use exact types 'classroom_storage_procedure' and 'digital_registration_record' for the corresponding commitments.\"\\n        },\\n        \"target\": {\\n          \"type\": \"string\"\\n        },\\n        \"detail\": {\\n          \"type\": \"string\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \"required\": [\\n        \"type\",\\n        \"target\",\\n        \"detail\"\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \"justification_fact_ids\": {\\n    \"type\": \"array\",\\n    \"items\": \"fact_id\"\\n  },\\n  \"revealed\": {\\n    \"type\": \"array\",\\n    \"items\": \"fact_id\"\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nRespond with ONLY a single JSON object representing your one action. No prose, no markdown, no explanation.,\"{\"\"type\"\": \"\"say\"\", \"\"text\"\": \"\"Good morning, everyone. Let's get started. As we discussed, we're looking at a six-week pilot to reduce classroom disruptions from student cell-phone use, covering grades 9 and 10, with phones placed in open classroom bins and a tentative launch date of September 2, 2026. Before I approve any student-facing procedures, I need each of you to report any operational information that might affect how we roll this out. Who would like to start?\"\"}\"\n"
